cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its curated flavor data, please cite this repository and the exact commit used."
title: "flavorwords — put this cup into words"
authors:
  - family-names: "Pan"
    given-names: "Dai"
    alias: "dpan538"
abstract: "A data product that turns what a coffee drinker tastes into a small, defensible flavor vocabulary. The corpus is 83,031 professional sensory assertions over 9,128 effective coffee records from eight reviewed source families, normalised to 94 canonical concepts and projected onto 12 flavor dimensions; sixteen owner-named reference profiles and measured context and answer matrices drive a deterministic, bilingual (zh-CN / en) inference with evidence labelling on every card. Shipped as an offline-capable, installable PWA at flavorwords.com, backed by a PostgreSQL 17 knowledge base with provenance and rights tracking."
repository-code: "https://github.com/dpan538/coffee-flavor-research"
url: "https://flavorwords.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - coffee
  - coffee flavor
  - flavor vocabulary
  - sensory science
  - sensory lexicon
  - data product
  - flavor vectors
  - knowledge base
  - PostgreSQL
  - bilingual
  - progressive web app
  - research software
